<label><input type="checkbox" name="hsts" value="1" <?=!empty($hddom['hsts'])?'checked':''?>> <b>HSTS</b> (2 years<?=((int)($hddom['hsts'] ?? 0) === 2)?', includeSubDomains':''?>) <small style="color:var(--muted)">Needs a valid certificate. Browsers then refuse plain HTTP <b>and any bad certificate on this host name, on every port</b>, for 2 years, and you cannot undo that from here. A self-signed service on the same name (e.g. OLS WebAdmin :7080) becomes unreachable by name: reach it by IP address or an SSH tunnel instead. Subdomains are not covered.</small></label><br>
<label><input type="checkbox" name="csp" value="1" <?=!empty($hddom['csp'])?'checked':''?>> <b>Content-Security-Policy</b> <small style="color:var(--muted)">Enforces frame-ancestors 'none' (the site can't be framed, even by itself), object-src 'none', base-uri/form-action 'self' (forms posting to another site stop working) and upgrade-insecure-requests. A stricter default-src 'self' policy runs report-only, so the browser console shows what it would block. Test the site after turning this on.</small></label><br>
<small style="color:var(--muted)">HSTS and CSP need the safe headers on. They are never turned on for all domains.</small><br>
